WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.569
-Good evening, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.137
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.005
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:09.476
There is only one week left
until the midterms.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:12.912
Said Biden,
"Um, cocaine is legal?"

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.851
President Biden
yesterday suggested a tax on

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:21.754
oil and gas companies if they do
not increase production,

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:24.390
because if anyone's concerned
about energy prices,

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:29.228
it's the guy who probably keeps
the thermostat at 78.

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.897
New York governor Kathy Hochul
is set to hold a rally

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:33.833
on Thursday with
Hillary Clinton.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.801
"Are you sure
that's a good idea?",

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:39.071
said Hillary Clinton.

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:40.873
President Biden spoke today
in Florida about

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.076
the importance of
Social Security and Medicare,

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.378
while Republicans
promised seniors

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.715
they'd just give them
that pool from "Cocoon."

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:59.392
A very, very fresh reference to
the film "Cocoon."

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.063
The New York City Council
last week

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.698
passed the so-called
Rat Action Plan

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.232
that aims to reduce
the number of rodents

00:01:07.232 --> 00:01:08.668
within the five boroughs.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.470
I guess they didn't have any
luck with their previous plan

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:15.808
of piling as much garbage
on the sidewalk as possible.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.511
Come on, guys!

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.113
Whose plan was that?

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.948
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.584
Was -- Be honest.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.953
Did a rat give you that plan?

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.822
"Uh...

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:32.691
he was a little fella."

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:34.861
CDC director
Dr. Rochelle Walensky,

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.262
over the weekend,
tested positive again

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.596
for the coronavirus.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:42.435
So, as per CDC recommendations,
she's taking a half-day.

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.071
In a recent interview,
singer Kid Rock said that

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:47.506
he would like to
have a beer with

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:49.075
former president Barack Obama

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.844
despite not liking
his policies or voting for him.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:54.580
In fact, Barack Obama doesn't
even need to be there.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.250
He'll just take
that beer, please.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.621
Utah Senator Mitt Romney
posted a picture yesterday

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:05.491
on Twitter of himself
dressed as Mario for Halloween,

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.727
because the scariest thing
he could think of

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:11.597
is a foreigner
taking our plumbing jobs.

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:15.568
A man in South Africa recently
broke a Guinness World Record

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:19.038
by doing 19 consecutive
backbends in one minute.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.507
Said the man, "Uh, right, yeah,
setting a world record.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.876
Uh, yeah, that's what
I was trying to do."

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.912
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.386
If you're wondering
what that joke means,

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.922
Mike Scollins wrote it.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.491
Just work backwards from that.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:45.164
And, finally,
Netflix's ad-supported plan

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:48.234
will launch this week
for just under $7 a month,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.503
though it will be
free for everyone on

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:53.272
the dad-supported plan.

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:56.843
Somehow, that's a dad joke
at the same time.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:03:00.613
"Are you still
on my dad-supported?"

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.050
Literally, like, what my dad
would call me up and say.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.321
"You know they're
doing ad-supported.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.790
Not you, though.
You're on the dad-supported."

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.226
That was a monologue.
What are you going to do?

